---
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";
import GuideList from "../../components/GuideList.astro";
import Simple from "../../layouts/Simple.astro";

const articles = (await getCollection("articles", ({ data }) => data.section === "guides")).sort(
  (a, b) => a.data.order - b.data.order,
);
---
<Simple
  title="Analytics guides"
  description="Practical guides to marketing attribution tools and cookieless analytics, written for founders choosing a stack."
  kicker="Guides"
  lede="These guides explain a decision, then compare the tools that can carry it. They are not a single ranked list of logos."
  crumbs={[{ href: "/", label: "Home" }, { label: "Guides" }]}
>
  <p>Attribution is the question of which visit should get credit for a payment. Cookieless analytics is the question of how stable that credit can be if you refuse a long-lived browser identifier. The two guides here answer them separately, because a cookieless script and a revenue report pull in opposite directions once a sale takes weeks instead of minutes.</p>
  <p>Both guides link to the tool pages on this site, including the <a href="/reviews/datafast/">DataFast review</a>, the <a href="/alternatives/google-analytics/">GA4 alternatives</a>, and the <a href="/pricing/posthog/">PostHog pricing notes</a>. Claims stay tied to vendor documentation checked on 24 November 2026.</p>
  <section slot="wide" class="band band-yellow">
    <div class="article-wide">
      <h2>Guides</h2>
      <GuideList
        items={articles.map((article) => ({
          href: `/${article.id}/`,
          title: article.data.title,
          description: article.data.description,
        }))}
      />
    </div>
  </section>
</Simple>
